Z||000000||ROB MAC||03-17-2000||07:30 PM||||one at a time I disconnected the headache...I mean headlight motor relays and sure enuff one was bad. All symptoms ( crackling and zap noise on radio , fluctuating idle, flickering lights and poor performance) went away. The driver side relay is on the inside front fender beside the headlight motor. The passenger side is on the motor mounting bracket between the motor and the coolant recovery bottle . Watch those knuckle scrapes cuz they're hard to reach.It's a small black thing with 2- 7mm screws holding it on and 2 wire harnesses going in the bottom. ||||reg||1
Z||000001||ROB MAC||03-23-2000||07:17 PM||||T'was the isolation relay and not the headlight relay causing the problem. I realized this as I was beating the crap outta it with a large hammer. Sorry for the faux pas.||||reg||1
